From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 16:18:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Include dlfcn.h only where it exists

The unguarded include breaks MinGW, which has no dlfcn.h; the platform
block below already includes it for Linux, BSD and AIX.

Upstream: not submitted; fixes the Windows/gcc port, not upstream OpenJDK
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hotspot/share/utilities/globalDefinitions_gcc.hpp | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/hotspot/share/utilities/globalDefinitions_gcc.hpp b/src/hotspot/share/utilities/globalDefinitions_gcc.hpp
index 5e1bcc198..38b9cd473 100644
--- a/src/hotspot/share/utilities/globalDefinitions_gcc.hpp
+++ b/src/hotspot/share/utilities/globalDefinitions_gcc.hpp
@@ -34,7 +34,6 @@
 #include "cppstdlib/cstdlib.hpp"
 
 #include <ctype.h>
-#include <dlfcn.h>
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <fcntl.h>
 #include <inttypes.h>
